  "final_answer": "I have gathered all the information needed to answer the question. Let me provide a comprehensive answer.\n\n## Answer\n\nBased on my review of Apple's official website (https://www.apple.com/apple-pencil/), there are **4 types of Apple Pencil** currently available on Apple's website:\n\n1. **Apple Pencil Pro** ($129) - The flagship model with advanced features\n2. **Apple Pencil (USB-C)** ($79) - The mid-range option\n3. **Apple Pencil (2nd generation)** - Available for older compatible iPads\n4. **Apple Pencil (1st generation)** - The original model (requires a USB-C to Apple Pencil Adapter for newer iPads with USB-C)\n\n### Which one supports Wireless pairing and charging?\n\nAccording to the Apple Pencil features comparison table on Apple's website:\n\n**Apple Pencil Pro** is the only model that supports **Wireless pairing and charging** — it \"automatically pairs and charges when attached\" magnetically to the side of a compatible iPad.\n\nThe other models do not support this feature:\n- **Apple Pencil (USB-C)**: Listed as \"Not compatible\" with wireless pairing and charging — it pairs and charges via a USB-C cable instead.\n- **Apple Pencil (1st and 2nd generation)**: Use Lightning/pairing methods that don't qualify as the wireless charging feature described.\n\nNote: The Apple Pencil Pro magnetically attaches to the side of compatible iPads (iPad Pro 13-inch and 11-inch M4/M5, iPad Air 13-inch and 11-inch M2/M3/M4, and iPad mini A17 Pro), where it pairs, charges, and is stored.",
